sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant F as Frontend (React)
    participant B as Backend (Flask REST API)
    participant D as Database (PostgreSQL)
    participant O as OpenAlex API
    participant N as NASA API
    participant A as AI provider API

    rect rgba(108, 140, 255, 0.10)
    Note over U,D: Part 1 - Browse and search research threads
    U->>F: Open Research Threads page
    F->>B: GET /research-threads
    B->>B: Middleware validates the request
    B->>D: Get all threads
    D-->>B: research_threads rows
    B-->>F: 200 OK {threads}
    F-->>U: Display thread cards
    U->>F: Enter a topic or pick a category
    F->>B: GET /research-threads with query and category
    B->>D: Search and filter threads
    D-->>B: Matching threads
    alt Results found
        B-->>F: 200 OK {threads}
        F-->>U: Display matching thread cards
    else No results
        B-->>F: 200 OK with an empty list
        F-->>U: Display the empty state
    end
    end

    rect rgba(43, 140, 126, 0.10)
    Note over U,N: Part 2 - Open a thread and explore its content
    U->>F: Select a research thread
    F->>B: GET /research-threads/{id}
    B->>D: Get overview, timeline events and chart data
    D-->>B: Thread, timeline_events and chart_data rows
    B->>O: Request related papers (cache first)
    O-->>B: Papers, authors and metadata
    B->>D: Save papers and link them to the thread
    B->>N: Request images and data for the topic (cache first)
    N-->>B: NASA images and data
    B-->>F: 200 OK {thread, timeline, papers, charts, nasaMedia}
    F-->>U: Display Overview, Timeline, Related Papers and NASA media
    end

    rect rgba(255, 181, 71, 0.12)
    Note over U,A: Part 3 - Ask the AI assistant about a paper
    U->>F: Select a paper and ask a question
    F->>B: POST /ai/explain {paperId, question}
    B->>D: Load paper from research_papers
    alt Paper is stored
        D-->>B: Paper
    else Paper is not stored
        D-->>B: Not found
        B->>O: Request the paper
        O-->>B: Paper and metadata
    end
    B->>A: Send the paper and the question
    alt AI provider responds
        A-->>B: Explanation
        B-->>F: 200 OK {explanation}
        F-->>U: Show the explanation in the chat
    else AI provider fails or times out
        A-->>B: Error or timeout
        B-->>F: JSON error
        F-->>U: Show the error state
    end
    end
